## Original Content
DÉCRYPTAGE - Alors que les pensions représentent un quart de la dépense publique, les candidats à la fonction suprême seront bien obligés de prendre position.

## Summary
The 2027 French presidential election is heavily influenced by the pensions issue, which is unavoidable for candidates. Pensions account for a significant portion of public spending, forcing candidates to address this divisive topic.

## Key Points
- The pensions issue is central to the 2027 French presidential campaign.
- Pensions represent 25% of public spending in France.
- Candidates are compelled to take a stand on pensions due to its impact.
- The issue is described as poisoning the campaign, indicating its divisive nature.


